verses.context:
>> 1 Thessalonians 4:1 Finally, brothers, we ask and encourage you in the Lord Jesus to live in a way that is pleasing to God, just as you have received from us. This is how you already live, so you should do so all the more.
   1 Thessalonians 4:2 For you know the instructions we gave you by the authority of the Lord Jesus.
   1 Thessalonians 4:3 For it is God’s will that you should be holy: You must abstain from sexual immorality;

   Matthew 5:36 Nor should you swear by your head, for you cannot make a single hair white or black.
   Matthew 5:37 Simply let your ‘Yes’ be ‘Yes,’ and your ‘No,’ ‘No.’ Anything more comes from the evil one.
>> Matthew 5:38 You have heard that it was said, ‘Eye for eye and tooth for tooth.’
   Matthew 5:39 But I tell you not to resist an evil person. If someone slaps you on your right cheek, turn to him the other also;
   Matthew 5:40 if someone wants to sue you and take your tunic, let him have your cloak as well;
